.Dd October 8, 2026
.Dt MANET-OS-CLEANUP.PY 8
.Os MANET
.Sh NAME
.Nm manet-os-cleanup.py
.Nd preview or apply the Raspberry Pi OS appliance cleanup
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -apply
.Op Fl -force
.Op Fl h | Fl -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
previews removal of unused build and desktop packages and disabling of
unused services on Raspberry Pi OS Trixie running a MANET kernel.
Run as root, including for a preview.
Without
.Fl -apply ,
it prints a JSON plan without changing packages or service policy.
.Pp
The removal plan protects MANET runtime dependencies and held packages.
Active swap, a dpkg audit error or proposed removal of a protected package
stops cleanup.
An applied cleanup also deletes the inactive stock swap file and downloaded
package cache.
It preserves operator cron jobs and required LVM maintenance.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -apply
Save inventories and the plan, stop and mask unused units, purge selected
packages and record successful completion.
A previously completed cleanup of the current profile is skipped.
.It Fl -force
With
.Fl -apply ,
repeat cleanup even if the current profile was completed previously.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print help and exit.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-os-cleanup/
Saved package inventories, removal plans, unit state and action logs.
.It Pa /var/lib/manet-os-cleanup/complete
Successfully applied cleanup profile.
.It Pa /var/swap
Stock swap file, removed only when unused and recognized as swap.
.It Pa /run/lock/manet-os-cleanup.lock
Lock serializing cleanup runs.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 after a successful preview, apply or skip.
Exits 1 on an operating error or failed safety check, and 2 for invalid
arguments.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Preview the plan:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
sudo manet-os-cleanup.py
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr radio-setup.sh 8
